PART 6: COMPONENT-BASED ARCHITECTURE

================================================================================

What is a Component?

A React component is a reusable piece of UI.

Component Feature       | Description
------------------------|----------------------------------------
Reusable                | Can be used multiple times
JavaScript-Based        | Commonly defined as a function
JSX                     | Can return JSX describing UI
State                    | Can use state
Props                    | Can receive input from a parent
Composable              | Components can contain other components


================================================================================

COMPONENT EXAMPLE

================================================================================

function MyButton({ label, onClick }) {

  return (
    <button onClick={onClick}>
      {label}
    </button>
  );
}


Use the component multiple times:

<MyButton
  label="Click Me"
  onClick={handleClick}
/>

<MyButton
  label="Submit"
  onClick={handleSubmit}
/>

<MyButton
  label="Cancel"
  onClick={handleCancel}
/>

Code Explanation
Code / Concept                    | Explanation
----------------------------------|-----------------------------------------
MyButton                          | Reusable component
label                             | Input used as button text
onClick                           | Input containing event handler
{label}                           | Displays passed label
onClick={onClick}                 | Uses passed click handler
<MyButton ... />                  | Uses/reuses the component


