PART 9: REACT'S ROLE IN MVC ARCHITECTURE

================================================================================

What is MVC?

MVC = Model View Controller

Layer       | Responsibility
------------|-------------------------------------------
Model       | Application data/domain state
View        | User interface
Controller  | Handles/co-ordinates application behavior


React has historically been described primarily as a View/UI library, rather than a complete MVC framework.

Simplified relationship:

DATA / MODEL
     ↓
APPLICATION LOGIC
     ↓
REACT UI
     ↓
USER

Why This Matters

React focuses primarily on building UI.

It can therefore be combined with:

APIs and different back ends.
Routing libraries/frameworks.
State management tools.
Data-fetching solutions.
Other JavaScript libraries.
Example
// Data
const user = {
  name: 'John',
  age: 30
};

// Application logic
function handleUserUpdate(newData) {
  // Update data
}

// React UI
<div>
  <h1>{user.name}</h1>
  <p>Age: {user.age}</p>
</div>


